From: Enceka <enceka@yeah.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: arbitrate shared native FE lifecycle ownership

Reserve idle native FE state for a lifecycle owner under ppe_lock. Keep
exact 64-bit generation and epoch across ambiguous QUIESCE completions,
and require an owner-specific acknowledgement before releasing the claim.

Block native policy activation, learning, health rearming and wired epoch
changes while claimed. Once quiesced, retain ordinary FLUSH and WLAN
retirement so global CT shutdown can finish before releasing the owner.

